export const title = "Combined Rule Condition Setting Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Combined Rule Condition Setting Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<p>For every event action setting, you can define combined rule conditions that must be satisfied in order for the action to fire when an event occurs.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 300\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <rect x=\"30\" y=\"120\" width=\"150\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f3f4f7\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"105\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">Event</text>\n  <line x1=\"180\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrC)\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"360\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"70\" ry=\"34\" fill=\"#eee3fb\" stroke=\"#b699e8\"/>\n  <text x=\"360\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a2c80\">Condition</text>\n  <line x1=\"430\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"540\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrC)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"430\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"540\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrC)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"430\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"540\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrC)\"/>\n  <rect x=\"540\" y=\"55\" width=\"150\" height=\"46\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#faebc0\" stroke=\"#d9b45c\"/>\n  <text x=\"615\" y=\"83\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7a5a13\">Action Handler</text>\n  <rect x=\"540\" y=\"127\" width=\"150\" height=\"46\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#faebc0\" stroke=\"#d9b45c\"/>\n  <text x=\"615\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7a5a13\">Action Handler</text>\n  <rect x=\"540\" y=\"197\" width=\"150\" height=\"46\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#faebc0\" stroke=\"#d9b45c\"/>\n  <text x=\"615\" y=\"225\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7a5a13\">Action Handler</text>\n  <line x1=\"360\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrC)\"/>\n  <text x=\"375\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#5b6270\">drop</text>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrC\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f9c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Combined Rule Condition Overview</h2>\n<p>When configuring an event action rule on any application, you can set conditions that govern when the action is triggered. Besides schedule-based conditions, you can also set conditions based on a range of other system states.</p>\n<p>You can use the state of a core system resource &mdash; such as an alarm input or virtual alarm input &mdash; to control a rule automatically. You can also use whether a previously configured event action has occurred as a condition.</p>\n<p>For example, suppose an intrusion event at a residence should switch on a warning light and broadcast a warning message from a camera. Configuring conditions like the ones below could help reduce false alarms:</p>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>Schedule (20:00&ndash;07:00)</li>\n<li>At least one person was detected outside the perimeter within the 10 seconds before the intrusion event</li>\n<li>Alarm Input 1 is currently active</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Setting Combined Rule Conditions</h2>\n<p>The following can be configured as a combined rule condition:</p>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>A rule configured on an application</li>\n<li>An individual event that makes up a rule configured on an application</li>\n<li>A system I/O device, such as an alarm input or virtual alarm input</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>You can add a new condition from the event action settings screen by clicking the <strong>Add</strong> button in the Combined Rule area.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:640px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:10px;\">\n    <span style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;\">Combined Rule</span>\n    <span class=\"btn small primary\">Add</span>\n  </div>\n  <table class=\"app-table\">\n    <tr><th>Reference Rule / Event</th><th>NOT</th><th>Time Range</th><th>I/O Status Reference</th><th>Operation</th></tr>\n    <tr><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"text-align:center;color:var(--text-muted);\">-</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:520px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:140px 1fr auto;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Reference UUID</span><input placeholder=\"UUID\" disabled><span class=\"btn small primary\">Search</span>\n    <span>NOT</span><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled><span></span>\n    <span>Time Range (In Secs)</span><span style=\"display:flex;gap:6px;align-items:center;\"><input value=\"-5\" disabled style=\"width:70px;\"> ~ <input value=\"0\" disabled style=\"width:70px;\"></span><span></span>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"text-align:right;margin-top:10px;\"><span class=\"btn small\">Cancel</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Apply</span></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Combined Rule condition editor</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>UUID</strong> &ndash; enter the UUID issued to the target event, rule, or system device. You can also click <strong>Search</strong> next to the UUID field to look up and select an already-configured item.</li>\n<li><strong>NOT</strong> &ndash; if checked, the condition is true when the referenced UUID's event or rule is <em>false</em>. For example, if you reference \"Event A\" and check NOT, the condition becomes true whenever Event A has not occurred.</li>\n<li><strong>Time Range</strong> &ndash; sets the valid time window (in seconds) for the referenced UUID's event or rule. If the referenced event occurs within this window, measured from when the rule's own event occurs, the condition is true.</li>\n<li><strong>I/O Status Reference</strong> &ndash; when set, the condition references the state of an I/O device. If the I/O device's state matches the configured state at the moment the rule's event occurs, the condition is true. This option is only available when the referenced item is an I/O device.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Setting System I/O Combined Conditions</h2>\n<p>Every rule from every application currently in use &mdash; along with each individual event that makes up those rules &mdash; can be referenced as a combined rule condition. Alarm inputs and virtual alarm inputs can always be used as a combined rule condition as well, without needing a separate event action rule configured for them first.</p>\n<p>When you configure an event action on an application, the event and the rule are each issued their own unique UUID. Enter the UUID of the event or rule you want to use as a condition, or click the Search button to look up and select an already-configured item.</p>\n<p>Alarm inputs and virtual alarm inputs each have a separate resource UUID assigned by default from the device's initial state, and the UUID search UI always lets you select I/O devices as a separate category.</p>\n<p>With a system I/O combined condition, you can set the condition to reference the state of the I/O device at the exact moment the primary event occurs.</p>";
